schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: "Local Nodes and DAOs: When (and Whether) to Formalize"
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    Distinguishes a local node (a community concept — people in a place,
    organized around shared purpose) from a DAO (a legal-and-technical
    form). Argues for "minimum viable coordination" (SuperBenefit's term)
    rather than building governance machinery pre-emptively. Names the three
    concrete things formalizing actually gives you (a treasury no one
    person controls, decisions anyone can verify, roles that survive
    people leaving), surveys which DAO tools are actually still standing as
    of mid-2026 (Safe, Snapshot/Snapshot X, Hats Protocol — with Tally and
    Coordinape flagged as having wound down), and recommends a hybrid
    model: informal/human for the social layer, onchain only for the parts
    that need a trust backstop.
  audience: local-node organizers deciding whether/how to formalize governance
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      formalizing to gain trust/legitimacy vs. formalizing as maintenance
      burden that "exhausts founders and quietly kills nodes" — the article
      argues structure should be added only in response to a named,
      current problem
  related_concepts:
    - DAO (Decentralized Autonomous Organization) vs. Local Node
  related_resources:
    - Snapshot
    - Hats Protocol
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/local-nodes-and-daos.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted

# assessed-but-excluded:
#   - Safe (multisig) is discussed extensively here but was NOT re-registered
#     as a separate resource object in this work order — it was already
#     ingested from the sibling local-node-model.md article in this same
#     batch (same run, same batch of 10) to avoid two near-identical "Safe"
#     resource candidates colliding on title-slug uniqueness.
#   - ReFi DAO and Greenpill Network are cited here as the hybrid model's
#     real-world examples (30+ nodes across 20+ countries; a dozen active
#     chapters) but not lifted as standalone resource objects — they
#     function as networks/case examples within this article rather than
#     the article's subject; a future ingest pass on refidao.com or
#     greenpill.network directly would be the right place to register them
#     properly (with return_path etc.) as source-systems.
